WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.000
Incredibly, Sony owns the film rights to more
than 900 Marvel Comics characters — a whole

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.680
laundry list of Spider-Man properties that
the studio plans to spin off into their own

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:09.680
cinematic universe.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.960
Here's the story behind every movie planned
for Sony's Spider-Verse.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.740
The first entry in Sony's elaborate plan for
an interconnected world of Spider-Man-based

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.900
films was 2018 blockbuster Venom.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.440
Critics were split on the quality of this
fairly odd film, which often played like a

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.640
dark mismatched-buddy-comedy in which both
roles were played by the same guy at the same

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.140
time.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:33.240
More important to Sony, however, is the fact
that Venom grossed $850 million at the worldwide

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:33.940
box office.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.300
“Well, you know, I aim to please."

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.579
Filmgoers clearly have an appetite for Venom,
so naturally the character will return in

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.200
Venom 2.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.960
And that might not be the end of it, either.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.000
Star Tom Hardy mentioned in 2018 that he's
contracted for a whole trilogy of Venom movies.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.420
Meanwhile, Venom screenwriter Jeff Pinkner
confirmed to Discussing Film in December that

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.540
he was already at work on the second installment.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.079
And in August 2019, Andy Serkis signed up
to direct.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:03.719
As for a release date, Venom 2 is highly likely
to be the mysterious "untitled Marvel sequel"

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.780
that Sony has penciled in for October 2020,
exactly two years after the debut of the first

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.280
film.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.240
While working to cure himself of a deadly
blood disorder, scientist Michael Morbius

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.000
manages to accidentally science himself into
becoming a vampire.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.380
Using his scientific expertise and his newly
acquired array of supernatural powers, the

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:25.429
character quickly found some success as a
tortured antihero, fighting his lust for blood

00:01:25.429 --> 00:01:27.580
while bringing vampiric justice to the night.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:32.340
First announced in 2017, production on Morbius
began in February 2019.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.380
Director Daniel Espinosa will direct from
a script by Matt Sazama and Burk Sharpless,

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:42.960
the creative minds behind Netflix's recent
Lost in Space reboot and 2014's Dracula Untold.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.439
Oscar winner Jared Leto stars as the bloodthirsty
protagonist, while Matt Smith co-stars as

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.660
his friend and fellow vampire Loxias Crown.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.100
Morbius hits movie theaters on July 31st 2020.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.479
Felicia Hardy, also known as the Black Cat,
has been a recurring foe and romantic interest

00:01:58.479 --> 00:02:03.389
for Peter Parker ever since her first appearance
in Amazing Spider-Man issue #194.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:07.529
A notorious cat burglar, Black Cat has the
power to manipulate the powers of probability

00:02:07.529 --> 00:02:08.100
and luck.

00:02:08.529 --> 00:02:12.520
She made a brief, out-of-costume appearance
in Amazing Spider-Man 2, but hasn't yet been

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.500
seen suited up on the big screen.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.820
Initially, Sony announced that Black Cat would
be getting a team-up movie with fellow occasional

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.610
Spider-Man ally Silver Sable.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:24.459
Tentatively titled Silver and Black and set
to be directed by Gina Prince-Bythewood, Sony

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:28.940
pulled the project from its release calendar
in 2018, in favor of solo movies for the two

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:29.440
heroes.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.640
According to Variety, Prince-Bythewood will
"likely" no longer direct but will stay on

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.940
as a producer for both individual movies.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.500
As for her replacement, all that's been reported
is that Sony really wants to go for a female

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.000
director.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.740
The other half of the canceled Silver and
Black project, Silver Sable is also headed

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.880
to the movies with her own announced solo
film.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:53.190
When she first showed up in Amazing Spider-Man
#265, Silver Sable appeared about as '80s

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:56.060
as you could get without actually starting
a glam-pop band.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.840
She's an assassin and mercenary from Eastern
Europe who wields guns, knives, and various

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.680
other accouterments with deadly accuracy.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.780
Like many characters in the Spider-Man mythos,
she also changes allegiances pretty frequently,

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.940
acting as both friend and foe to the friendly
neighborhood wall-crawler.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.960
This is another project with few details to
report at the moment, as there have been real

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:19.430
hints as to anyone who might be involved — apart
from Gina Prince-Bythewood's position as producer.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:25.560
Kraven the Hunter first popped up in Amazing
Spider-Man #15 all the way back in 1964.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.989
In fact, he goes back so far that he was even
a member of the original Sinister Six, making

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:34.389
him the oldest Marvel character currently
projected to get his own Spider-Verse movie.

00:03:34.389 --> 00:03:38.650
A Russian expat with a unique flair for clothes
made out of lion faces, Kraven is a big game

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.660
hunter obsessed with proving that he can kill
anything — and, in particular, Spider-Man.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.940
"Where do all these guys come from?"

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.260
Unfortunately, backstory on the character
is just about all we have on Sony's Kraven

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.160
the Hunter movie.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:54.311
Not a lot is known about the upcoming film
adaptation, except that The Equalizer 2 and

00:03:54.311 --> 00:03:58.099
Jack Reacher: Never Go Back writer Richard
Wenk was hired to write the script back in

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.240
August 2018.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.420
A couple of months later, Wenk teased a very
special appearance in the film, claiming in

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.640
an interview with Discussing Film that Kraven
will come face-to-face with Spider-Man himself.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.139
Sony isn't just planning on bringing the heavy-hitters
to their Spider-Verse, though — they've

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.280
also got plans for some of Marvel's more obscure
Spider-Man characters.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:19.920
Cindy Moon has actually appeared briefly in
the MCU, but her comic alter-ego Silk has

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.350
yet to be explored on film.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:25.270
In the comics, a retcon explained that Cindy
was bitten by the same radioactive spider

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:27.880
as Peter and ended up with very similar powers.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.630
Little development has been reported on the
project, aside from the major announcement

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:37.380
in 2018 that longtime Sony producer and Spider-properties
shepherd Amy Pascal was attached to produce.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:42.120
Pascal's 2019 departure from the company,
however, has thrown the project into doubt.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.240
Then you've got Jackpot: a scientist, mom,
and all-around super-strong crimefighting

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:46.740
boss.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:51.200
The details behind the purported Jackpot movie
are pretty mysterious, with Sony still in

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.590
the process of finding a screenwriter to take
on, so it's safe to assume it'll be a while

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.120
before Jackpot hits theaters.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.360
Finally, there's a rumor swirling around that
Spike Lee is in line to direct Sonyl's upcoming

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.260
Nightwatch movie, with Luke Cage showrunner
Cheo Hodari Coker said to be a top candidate

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:09.680
for writing duties — but that's about all
anyone knows about that one, too.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.380
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse is a truly
special movie.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:18.000
It won an Oscar for Best Animated Feature,
outranked every other Spider-Man movie on

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.889
Rotten Tomatoes, and earned nearly $200 million
at the domestic box office.

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:25.520
The world clearly wants more trips through
time and space with Miles Morales and his

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.900
friends — and, luckily, a sequel is indeed
in the works.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:32.900
Sony announced big plans for the animated
sector of its Marvel slate in November 2018,

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.910
before Into the Spider-Verse had even hit
theaters.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:39.580
Avatar: The Last Airbender veteran Joaquim
Dos Santos has signed on to direct the film,

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.220
with Wonder Woman 1984 and Zombieland 2 writer
David Callaham handling the script.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.480
“That's all, folks."

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:47.500
"Is he allowed to say that?

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:48.320
Legally?"

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.699
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse was particularly
noteworthy for spotlighting a biracial teen

00:05:55.780 --> 00:06:00.120
superhero in Miles Morales alongside a stand-out
female lead in Gwen Stacy.

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.880
And now the latter is set to get her own animated
spinoff.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.820
Before Into the Spider-Verse hit theaters,
Sony announced that it had started work on

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:09.180
a film about three generations of Spider women.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:13.640
Spider-Gwen will return from the first movie,
assisted in her adventures by another Spider-Woman,

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.820
Jessica Drew, and Silk.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:19.580
Sony has hired Bek Smith to pen the screenplay
and DC animation veteran Lauren Montgomery

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:22.100
to direct, but more details have yet to be
confirmed.

